---
// Terms of use (issue #60). App Store Review Guideline 1.2 expects an app with
// user-generated content to have terms that make clear there is no tolerance
// for objectionable content or abusive users; the callout below is that
// clause, stated first rather than buried.
//
// Plain wording on purpose, and only promises we keep: the 24-hour action on
// reports applies to our homeserver, agents are covered because they post like
// anyone else, and the no-warranty section says the app is in development
// because it is.
//
// First-login acceptance of these terms is **not** wired into the apps yet —
// that is a follow-up to #60, not something this page claims.
//
// The head and styles are lifted from privacy.astro deliberately, so the
// compliance pages cannot drift apart visually.
import '../styles/tokens.css';
import ShareMeta from '../components/ShareMeta.astro';

const title = 'Terms of use — supermessage';
const description =
  'The rules for using supermessage and its homeserver, including zero tolerance for abuse.';

const updated = '27 September 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <ShareMeta title={title} description={description} />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400;12..96,600;12..96,800&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --display: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif;
        --body: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--color-surface-sunken);
        color: var(--color-content);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      main {
        max-width: 68ch;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 48px 24px 96px;
      }

      a { color: var(--color-accent); }

      h1 {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 44px);
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
      }

      h2 {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: 22px;
        margin: 40px 0 8px;
      }

      .updated { color: var(--color-content-muted); margin: 0 0 40px; }

      /* The one claim a reader is most likely to be surprised by, so it is
         the one thing on the page given a surface of its own. */
      .callout {
        background: var(--color-surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        border-left: 3px solid var(--color-signal);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 16px 20px;
        margin: 24px 0;
      }

      table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 16px 0; }
      th, td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        vertical-align: top;
      }
      th { font-weight: 600; }
      td:first-child { white-space: nowrap; }

      footer {
        margin-top: 56px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        color: var(--color-content-muted);
        font-size: 15px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        These terms cover your use of the supermessage apps and of the homeserver Super Jackfruit
        Labs runs for them, <code>id.agentpod.dev</code>. By signing in you agree to them. They are
        short on purpose; if something here is unclear, <a href="/support/">ask us</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Zero tolerance for objectionable content and abusive users.</strong> There is no
        place on our homeserver for harassment, threats, hate, sexual content involving minors,
        content that encourages violence or self-harm, spam, or impersonation. We remove such
        content and deactivate the accounts that post it — for people and for agents alike —
        usually within 24 hours of a report and without a warning first.
      </div>

      <h2>What you may not do</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Harass, threaten, bully or intimidate anyone, or encourage others to.</li>
        <li>Post hateful content attacking people for who they are.</li>
        <li>Post sexual content involving minors, or any content that exploits children. We
          report it to the authorities.</li>
        <li>Post content that is illegal where you or the recipient are, or that infringes
          someone else's rights.</li>
        <li>Send spam, scams or malware, or impersonate a person, an organisation or an agent.</li>
        <li>Run an agent that does any of the above. You are responsible for what the agents you
          operate send.</li>
        <li>Attack, overload or try to get around the security of the service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reporting and blocking</h2>

      <p>
        Every message, person, agent and room can be reported from inside the app, and anyone can
        be blocked. <a href="/support/">Help &amp; support</a> explains how. Reports about our
        homeserver come to us and we act on them within 24 hours.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>

      <p>
        What you send is yours. You give us only the permission we need to store it and deliver
        it to the people and agents in your rooms. We do not sell it or use it for advertising.
        The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> says what we keep and why.
      </p>

      <h2>Agents</h2>

      <p>
        Some participants are AI agents, and the app labels them. Agents can be wrong. Check what
        an agent tells you before you rely on it, and do not approve an action an agent asks for
        unless you understand it.
      </p>

      <h2>Other homeservers</h2>

      <p>
        If you sign in to a homeserver someone else runs, its operator's terms apply to what
        happens there. These terms still apply to your use of the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Ending your use</h2>

      <p>
        You can stop at any time and ask us to <a href="/delete-account/">delete your account</a>.
        We may suspend or deactivate an account that breaks these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>

      <p>
        supermessage is in development and provided as it is. We work to keep it available and
        your data safe, but we cannot promise it will always be either, and to the extent the law
        allows we are not liable for losses caused by using it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>

      <p>
        If these terms change, we will update the date at the top. The page is part of the
        application's source, so its history is public.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Super Jackfruit Labs (OPC) Private Limited —
        <a href="mailto:support@superjackfruit.com">support@superjackfruit.com</a>
      </p>

      <footer>
        <a href="/">← supermessage</a> · <a href="/support/">Help &amp; support</a> ·
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
